  "content": {
    "id": "p38-q40-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "40",
    "prompt": "The sum of the first 5 terms of an arithmetic sequence is 110 and the sum of the first 10 terms is 320. Find the first term and the common difference.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "First term $14$; common difference $4$.",
      "worked": "$S_5=110$, $S_{10}=320$.\n$$\\begin{align*}S_5=\\frac52[2a+4d]&=110\\\\5(2a+4d)&=220\\\\2a+4d&=44\\\\a+2d&=22\\qquad(1)\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}S_{10}=\\frac{10}{2}[2a+9d]&=320\\\\5(2a+9d)&=320\\\\2a+9d&=64\\qquad(2)\\end{align*}$$\n$(2)-2(1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}(2a+9d)-2(a+2d)&=64-44\\\\5d&=20\\\\d&=4\\end{align*}$$\nSubstitute into $(1)$:\n$$\\begin{align*}a+8&=22\\\\a&=14\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore $a=14$, $d=4$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
